{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>How is the gold dimmed</b> – Some say יועם is like חשך; the Targum of וְהִנֵה כֵהָה הַנֶּגַע (Leviticus 13:6) is עֲמִיָּא מִכְתְּשָׁא. But what seems right to me is like לֹא יַעֲמִיטֵהוּ (Ezekiel 31:8), and its pattern is like לֶחֶם יוּדָק (Isaiah 28:28)."], :book :lamentations, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra writes לא עממוהו but cites Ezekiel 31:8; the verse reads לא יעמיטהו; translated the form as Ibn Ezra cites it. Also his Isaiah citation reads לחם ידק, but the verse has יוּדָק; preserved his spelling."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Lamentations -- Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%9E%D7%92%D7%99%D7%9C%D7%AA_%D7%90%D7%99%D7%9B%D7%94"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:00.555891300Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}